1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,446
Minus twenty degrees of freezing cold...

2
00:00:02,716 --> 00:00:05,718
A snowstorm all around, a bone-biting wind.

3
00:00:06,091 --> 00:00:11,457
In weather like that, do you know what happens if a normal person steps out without clothes?

4
00:00:11,737 --> 00:00:15,165
In just five to ten minutes, the blood vessels constrict.

5
00:00:15,531 --> 00:00:20,579
After twenty minutes, body temperature drops dangerously and hypothermia sets in.

6
00:00:20,941 --> 00:00:26,538
Within half an hour, the heart stops and the body freezes like an ice doll and dies!

7
00:00:26,888 --> 00:00:29,642
This is an absolute rule written by medical science!

8
00:00:30,097 --> 00:00:33,958
But... on that same minus-twenty-degree Himalayan snow...

9
00:00:34,134 --> 00:00:40,345
what if monks sit for hours with nothing on but a thin cotton cloth?

10
00:00:40,618 --> 00:00:44,180
And if cloths soaked in ice water are draped over their bodies...

11
00:00:44,374 --> 00:00:49,906
what if, instead of freezing, those wet cloths steam and dry from their body heat?

12
00:00:50,370 --> 00:00:53,612
Hello everyone, welcome to Be Practical With Kishore!

13
00:00:53,971 --> 00:00:55,186
This is not just a story...

14
00:00:55,424 --> 00:01:03,782
It's an absolute reality that world-famous Harvard University medical scientists tested themselves in the hills of Ladakh and showed the world!

15
00:01:04,170 --> 00:01:07,388
Meanwhile in Europe, a man named Wim Hof...

16
00:01:07,417 --> 00:01:10,939
runs through Arctic Circle snow wearing only shorts,

17
00:01:11,197 --> 00:01:15,630
sits neck-deep in a box of pure ice cubes for two hours,

18
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:21,809
and even with dangerous bacteria injected into his blood, he neutralises it with his internal heat!

19
00:01:22,067 --> 00:01:26,784
How can a fire blaze inside the human body in freezing snow?

20
00:01:27,006 --> 00:01:30,702
How can human willpower control body temperature?

21
00:01:30,974 --> 00:01:34,929
Let us practically break down the science of fire and ice!

